  "result": "Perfect! All 126 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Summary of VAT Implementation:**\n\n**Changes to src/invoices.js:**\n- Imported `roundCents` from src/money.js for proper VAT rounding\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to calculate VAT per line on the discounted amount\n- VAT is rounded per line (not on invoice total)\n- Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n\n**VAT Calculation Logic:**\n- For each line: `discounted_amount = line_total - (line_total \u00d7 discountPercent / 100)`\n- For each line: `line_vat = roundCents(discounted_amount \u00d7 vatRate / 100)`\n- `vat = sum of all line VATs` (not a percentage of invoice total)\n- Amounts clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\n**Changes to src/render.js:**\n- Shows VAT line when present: `VAT: +\u20acXXX.XX`\n- Shows `Subtotal:` and `Discount:` lines when discounts or VAT exist\n- Renders VAT before the Total line\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- 13 new VAT tests in test/invoices.test.js covering:\n  - VAT without discounts\n  - VAT with discounts (single and multiple lines)\n  - Different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - VAT rounding per line\n  - Tier discounts with VAT\n  \n- 5 new VAT tests in test/render.test.js covering:\n  - Rendering VAT amounts\n  - Zero-rated items\n  - VAT with discounts and tier discounts\n\nAll 126 tests pass successfully!",
